{
  "slug": "experiments",
  "group": "start",
  "layout": "wide",
  "title": {
    "zh": "实验结果",
    "en": "Experimental results"
  },
  "description": {
    "zh": "以 GLM-5-turbo 为统一基座模型，对比不同智能体运行框架（agent harness）在图检索、图论、图机器学习和图开放式问答中的任务成功率。",
    "en": "Task success rates for graph retrieval, graph theory, graph machine learning, and open-ended graph question answering, comparing agent harnesses with GLM-5-turbo as the shared base model."
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "reading-the-results",
      "title": {
        "zh": "如何读表",
        "en": "Reading the results"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": {
            "zh": "所有实验均使用 GLM-5-turbo 作为基座模型；行名表示 agent harness。原始结果中只写模型名的行对应 OpenClaw。表中仅保留 SR（任务成功率），统一换算为百分数并保留两位小数，数值越高越好。",
            "en": "All experiments use GLM-5-turbo as the base model; rows identify the agent harness. A model-only row in the source results denotes OpenClaw. Only SR (task success rate) is reported, as a percentage with two decimal places; higher is better."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": {
            "zh": "每列单独比较：最高分加粗，次高分加下划线；并列成绩使用相同标记。图检索和图论各比较 OpenClaw、iGraph；图机器学习和图开放式问答各比较 Hermes、Claude Code、OpenClaw、iGraph。",
            "en": "Scores are ranked independently within each column: the highest score is bold, the second-highest score is underlined, and ties receive the same marking. Retrieval and theory compare OpenClaw and iGraph; machine learning and open-ended question answering compare Hermes, Claude Code, OpenClaw, and iGraph."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "zh": "NAG：数值属性图（Numerical-Attribute Graph）。",
              "en": "NAG: Numerical-Attribute Graph."
            },
            {
              "zh": "TAG：文本属性图（Text-Attributed Graph）。",
              "en": "TAG: Text-Attributed Graph."
            },
            {
              "zh": "TPG：文本配对图（Text-Paired Graph）。",
              "en": "TPG: Text-Paired Graph."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
